       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine. The usual adult range is 2.5\u201310 mg once daily, and 10 mg is the ceiling. A dose of 50 mg risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Amlodipine's long half-life means those effects can last a long time, and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema is also possible.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, a typical starting dose\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, for a frail patient or a more cautious start\n\nIf 50 mg is intentional, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note documenting that. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
